.TH LESS 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
less \- browse a file or piped input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
less [file]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Browse a file, or standard input if no file is given. Space or f advances
one screen; b goes back one screen; j and k move one line; d and u move
half a screen; g returns to the start; Enter moves down one line; q quits.
Ctrl-C interrupts and restores the terminal.
.PP
Piped input is spooled to an unlinked temporary file for backward movement.
With redirected output, less copies the input unchanged. The line index
is bounded by available memory, and older positions may be discarded.
Search commands are not implemented in this small pager.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
LINES and COLUMNS override the terminal size. The fallback is 24 by 80.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
less README
seq 1 100 | less
.fi
